D 75th: an exported function name over-counts by one in `distpred` (use a string literal for a CTL row); the census tool's box copy is never used (run the local file through `boxrun`); upload tools never overwrite; each verify POST, even a refused one, writes one `audit_logs` row (say "users equal", not "audit equal"). D 76th: re-keying leaves target-box constants where a token grep does not look: grep every 40-hex, ISO and number literal against Kintsugi's values; zsh `set -- $spec` does not split (bash heredoc). D 77th: a re-keyed kit keeps the OLD ordinal in watcher selftest and vault-commit markers; zsh `for t in $L` does not split and an unmatched glob aborts the call (run loops as `bash <<'EOF'`); **a blanket `docker compose up -d` recreates every REDIS_URL reader including anchoring: targeted `--no-deps --force-recreate <svc>` only**. D 78th: `ps | grep -F token` counts the grep itself (bracket regex).

