- *Request 2 (documentId strategy, the other route the PR changed):* ONE `POST` body `{"documentId": "00a56a95-800d-4f75-8769-cb173a40b1ab"}` and ONE with Obeden's id as control. **PASS:** each answers 200 with exactly one match for its own id. ISS3's pre-fix answer (zero, the lookup ran under the request's tenant) is READ FROM THE CODE, not measured: UNMEASURED unless Wednesday rules W7.
- *Side effects (licence D79-W6):* each POST writes ONE `audit_logs` row (`v2.verify`, user null; D 75th measured +1 per v2 POST) and NO billing row (users, billing_charge_events, charge_events, billing_credit_grants, documents all equal; Kam 2026-11-16 09:59:15, card `secuura-cert-verify-anonymous-billing-1116` = a, "No charge for anonymous calls"). Three POSTs = +3 audit rows, no anchor, no document, no charge. Count before and after and say whether each write appeared.
**LC2. KS-2280 (PR 2263): the gateway's boot role check, flag UNSET.** In the NEW gateway's log since its StartedAt, the count of lines containing `(KS-2280)` is **0 expected**: the role is `secuura_app | false | false` (`REC75/evidence/phase2/gateway_runtime_role.txt`), the verdict is `ok`, and `ok` prints nothing. A WARNING line is a FINDING (role changed or read failed), not a fix. **Controls (required):** (i) the same count command returns 1 for `[Redis] Connecting` and 0 for a nonsense string; (ii) `KS-2280` is present in the new image's compiled gateway and absent in `dev-api-gateway:pre-<tag>` (section 7); (iii) D 75th's read-only `p2role` re-run (one SELECT on `pg_roles` through the container's own `DATABASE_URL`, three columns printed, nothing left) reads `secuura_app | f | f` again. **`DB_ROLE_GUARD` is never set; assert it UNSET by name in the container, with a control.** Limit: the `ok` verdict leaves no trace; warn and refuse are unit-proven only (gate 386).
**LC3. KS-1936 (PR 2260): the admin route.** The PR's claim is "a non-platform role gets 403". Every discriminating probe needs an ORG_ADMIN or ISSUER_ADMIN token and no login or minted token is licensed: **the 403 is UNMEASURED live, unit-proven only** (cells in `ks1936-identity-level-route-is-platform-only.test.ts`, gates 382/383). Measurable and safe: image content (section 7), and ONE unauthenticated `PATCH /api/admin/identity/users/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/level` body `{"verificationLevel": 1}` answering 401 (requireAdmin runs first; no query, no write), labelled a control that the front door is unchanged (the old build answers the same). A real 403 needs a Kam-issued ORG_ADMIN session: W8.
